<%# The target is the listing's RESOLVED identity, not the raw `storage_id`: the DataTable
    sanitizes it into a valid CSS identifier, so a storage_id with "/", with spaces or
    starting with a digit yields a different id. Turbo resolves the target through
    getElementById: with no node it replaces nothing, does not blow up and does not log.
    The body is the SAME partial as the html.erb, so the two paths cannot diverge. %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace Bali::DataTable::ListingIdentity.for(@filter_form) do %>
  <%= render 'listing' %>
<% end %>
